### Applicability of Assisted Replication to EVPN SRv6 Services
* **Presenter:** Jorge Rabadan
* **Slide Deck:** [ietf127-bess-evpn-srv6-ar-00](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bess-ietf127-bess-evpn-srv6-ar-00-00)
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bess-evpn-srv6-ar`
* **Discussion:**
  * The draft defines procedures for using Assisted Replication (RFC 9574) in EVPN SRv6 networks. It introduces a new SRv6 Endpoint behavior, `N.DT2MAR`.
  * When a replicator receives packets at the `N.DT2MAR` endpoint, it decapsulates, performs local flooding, and re-encapsulates traffic to remote EVPN SRv6 destinations with source squelching.
  * Himanshu Shah inquired how multihomed source ESI filtering is handled on the replicator. Jorge explained that multihoming can be handled via control-plane mechanisms (Extended Assisted Replication) or local bias while preserving the source IP.

