### EVPN Anycast Multihoming / Aliasing
* **Presenter:** Jorge Rabadan
* **Slide Deck:** [ietf127-bess-evpn-anycast-multihoming-06](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bess-ietf127-bess-evpn-anycast-multihoming-06-00)
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bess-evpn-anycast-aliasing`
* **Discussion:**
  * Enhances all-active multihoming in NVO3 environments using an Anycast VTEP. Remote PEs see a single destination Next Hop for the Anycast VTEP, eliminating the need for Ethernet Auto-Discovery (AD) per-EVI routes.
  * Revision updates clarify local switching behavior on egress PEs (using unicast VTEP IP during local access failures), error handling procedures, and fast-reroute scope.
  * Krishna Swamy asked about carrying Router MACs per-switch/system versus per-tenant in AD per-ES routes. Jorge agreed to follow up offline to refine the text.

