### Group Policy ID in EVPN
* **Presenter:** Ali Sajassi
* **Slide Deck:** [draft-lrss-bess-evpn-group-policy](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bess-draft-lrss-bess-evpn-group-policy-00)
* **Draft:** `draft-lrss-bess-evpn-group-policy`
* **Discussion:**
  * Defines micro-segmentation capabilities within a tenant/VRF using Group Policy IDs (GPI) in EVPN, targeted at multi-tier enterprise applications, data centers, and AI/GPU cluster workloads.
  * Introduces a 4-bit Flag field in BGP EVPN signaling (with 1 bit explicitly signaling data-plane GPI support) to ensure deterministic policy enforcement between ingress and egress PEs.
  * Israel Means asked how policy inconsistencies during network convergence are handled. Ali explained that PEs fall back to a configured default mode policy when unknown or inconsistent policy tags are encountered.
  * The draft was previously held pending progress on companion encapsulation specifications; Ali requested working group adoption now that dependencies are clear.

