### Fast Convergence in EVPN / MVPN Multicast Multihoming
* **Presenter:** Ali Sajassi
* **Slide Deck:** [draft-vgovindan-bess-evpn-mvpn-seamles-mh-converge-00](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bess-draft-vgovindan-bess-evpn-mvpn-seamles-mh-converge-00-00)
* **Draft:** `draft-vgovindan-bess-evpn-mvpn-seamles-mh-converge-00`
* **Discussion:**
  * Proposes an extension to [`draft-ietf-bess-evpn-mvpn-seamless-interop`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-bess-evpn-mvpn-seamless-interop) to improve failover convergence times for all-active multihoming.
  * Egress PEs advertise overlay multicast state attached to a list of Route Targets for all PEs in the multihoming group. This pre-builds state across all multihomed PEs prior to any link or node failure.
  * Jorge Rabadan noted that pre-building state improves convergence and helps prevent packet duplication during failover events.

