### Exporting BGP VPN Information in IPFIX
* **Presenter:** Yao Liu
* **Slide Deck:** [draft-liu-bess-ipfix-bgp-vpn](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bess-draft-liu-bess-ipfix-bgp-vpn-00)
* **Draft:** `draft-liu-bess-ipfix-bgp-vpn`
* **Discussion:**
  * Defines four new IPFIX Information Elements (IEs): BGP VPN Next Hop IPv4/IPv6 addresses, SRv6 VPN Service SID, and SRv6 Service SID Locator Length.
  * Stephane Litkowski and Ali Sajassi questioned the necessity of dedicated VPN Next Hop IEs, suggesting that standard BGP Next Hop IEs already carry the egress PE address matched by the data plane.
  * Sasha Vainshtein commented that in Option B inter-AS scenarios, the BGP Next Hop changes across domain boundaries, making VPN egress attribution complex. The authors will refine the draft based on the feedback.

